{#- One use case, rendered from an entry in usecases.yml. Included inside a loop
    that has set `case`, by the Use-Cases page and by each industry page for the
    cases that belong to its sector. Nunjucks includes see the caller's variables,
    which is why this can be a partial rather than a macro.

    Pulled out of use-cases.njk on 2 Sep 2026 when the industry pages needed the
    same card. The alternative was a second copy of the markup, which would have
    given the two places a chance to drift; the same reasoning that put How It
    Works into a partial. The Use-Cases page renders byte-for-byte as it did
    before the extraction. -#}
    <article class="usecase">
      <div class="usecase-media">
        <img src="{{ case.image }}" alt="{{ case.image_alt }}" loading="lazy">
      </div>
      <div class="usecase-body">
        <span class="usecase-sector">{{ case.sector }}</span>
        <h3>{{ case.title }}</h3>
        <div class="usecase-block">
          <h4>{{ usecases.cases.challenge_label }}</h4>
          <p>{{ case.challenge }}</p>
        </div>
        <div class="usecase-block">
          <h4>{{ usecases.cases.solution_label }}</h4>
          <p>{{ case.solution }}</p>
        </div>
        <div class="usecase-block is-outcome">
          <h4>{{ usecases.cases.outcome_label }}</h4>
          <p>{{ case.outcome }}</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>
